.Dd September 2, 2026
.Dt NG_MODBUS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ng_modbus
.Nd Modbus protocol engine in netgraph
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm ngctl
.Ar create
.Ar modbus
.Nm ngctl
.Ar config
.Ar modbus
.Cm setconfig
.Op Ar role Ar = Ns Ar N
.Op Ar transport Ar = Ns Ar N
.Op Ar unit_id Ar = Ns Ar N
.Nm ngctl
.Ar config
.Ar modbus
.Cm request
.Ar pdu Ar = Ns Ar N
.Ar pdulen Ar = Ns Ar N
.Ar unit_id Ar = Ns Ar N
.Ar tid Ar = Ns Ar N
.Nm ngctl
.Ar config
.Ar modbus
.Cm setbackend
.Ar ncoils Ar = Ns Ar N
.Ar ndiscrete_in Ar = Ns Ar N
.Ar ninput_regs Ar = Ns Ar N
.Ar nholding_regs Ar = Ns Ar N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
node type implements a Modbus server or client.
It registers the type
.Li modbus
when the module is loaded and unregisters it when the module is unloaded.
.Pp
The protocol engine is independent of the transport.
Requests are decoded from a request PDU, executed against a register
backend, and answered with a response PDU;
Modbus/TCP, RTU and ASCII add only their own framing around it.
.Pp
The node has one hook:
.Bl -tag -width "lower" -compact
.It Li lower
Transport data.
A peer supplies or receives the framed bytes described by
.Cm transport .
.El
.Pp
Control messages are addressed to the node itself and do not need a hook.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Bl -tag -width "setconfig" -compact
.It Cm setconfig role= Ns Ar N transport= Ns Ar N unit_id= Ns Ar N
Set the role, the framing and the unit identifier.
.Cm role
is
.Dv MODBUS_ROLE_SERVER
(1) or
.Dv MODBUS_ROLE_CLIENT
(2).
.Cm transport
is one of
.Dv NONE
(0), which carries one bare PDU per item and exists for testing,
.Dv VNET
(1),
.Dv TCP
(2), which uses the MBAP header,
.Dv RTU
(3), which uses the CRC framing, or
.Dv ASCII
(4), which uses the LRC framing.
.Cm unit_id
is this node's address, 0 for broadcast or 1 to 247.
The specification reserves 248 to 255, and a configuration outside those
bounds is refused.
.It Cm getconfig
Return the current configuration.
.It Cm setbackend ncoils= Ns Ar N ndiscrete_in= Ns Ar N ninput_regs= Ns Ar N nholding_regs= Ns Ar N
Resize the four register areas.
Each must be between 1 and 4096; a rejected size leaves the existing map
untouched.
.It Cm getbackend
Return the current sizes.
.It Cm request pdu= Ns Ar N pdulen= Ns Ar N unit_id= Ns Ar N tid= Ns Ar N
Issue one request as a client.
.Cm pdu
is the request PDU, without any framing, and
.Cm pdulen
its length.
.Cm unit_id
is the slave to address and
.Cm tid
the transaction identifier used by Modbus/TCP.
A request is refused with EBUSY while another is still outstanding.
.It Cm getresponse
Return the response of the last client request:
its state, which is one of idle, pending, done, expired or failed, and the
response PDU when one was accepted.
.It Cm getinfo
Return the ABI version, the maximum PDU size, the largest ADU of the
framings this build supports, the set of supported framings, and the default
serial line parameters.
.It Cm getstats
Return the counters described in
.Sx STATISTICS .
.It Cm clrstats
Zero the counters.
.El
.Sh DATA PATH
Each item received on the
.Li lower
hook is fed to the configured framing one byte at a time, because a TCP
stream, and a serial line, carry no packet boundaries.
The framings own no timer: the RTU framing recognises a frame by its CRC, and
reports the inter-character deadlines it computes for the node to act on.
.Pp
A request addressed to another unit identifier is ignored.
A broadcast request, unit identifier zero, is executed but never answered,
and a node configured with unit identifier zero answers nothing.
.Pp
Responses are framed the way the request arrived:
an MBAP header carrying the request's transaction identifier for
.Cm transport=TCP ,
the unit address and the CRC for
.Cm transport=RTU ,
and a colon, hexadecimal characters, the LRC and CR LF for
.Cm transport=ASCII .
For
.Cm transport=NONE
and
.Cm transport=VNET
the response is the bare response PDU.
.Sh FUNCTION CODES
The following function codes are implemented:
.Bl -tag -width "17 (0x17)" -compact
.It 1 (0x01)
Read Coils
.It 2 (0x02)
Read Discrete Inputs
.It 3 (0x03)
Read Holding Registers
.It 4 (0x04)
Read Input Registers
.It 5 (0x05)
Write Single Coil
.It 6 (0x06)
Write Single Register
.It 15 (0x0F)
Write Multiple Coils
.It 16 (0x10)
Write Multiple Registers
.It 22 (0x16)
Mask Write Register
.It 23 (0x17)
Read/Write Multiple Registers
.El
.Pp
Any other function code is answered with exception code 1,
ILLEGAL FUNCTION.
Requests that violate a length, quantity or byte count rule are answered with
exception code 3,
ILLEGAL DATA VALUE,
and addresses outside the configured map with exception code 2,
ILLEGAL DATA ADDRESS.
The remaining exception codes of the specification are defined but never
generated by this implementation.
.Sh STATISTICS
.Bl -tag -width "rx_frames" -compact
.It Li rx_frames
Items received on the lower hook.
.It Li rx_bytes
Bytes received on the lower hook.
.It Li tx_frames
Response frames transmitted.
.It Li tx_bytes
Bytes transmitted.
.It Li errors
Malformed frames, CRC and LRC failures, invalid function codes, protocol
exceptions, allocation failures and rejected items.
.El
.Pp
A client transaction also counts as
.Dv errors
when the response cannot be used.
.It Li timeouts
Client transactions that expired with no response.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a server holding 1024 coils and holding registers, and answer a
Modbus/TCP peer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload modbus
ngctl create modbus
ngctl config modbus setconfig role=1 transport=2 unit_id=1
ngctl config modbus setbackend ncoils=1024 nholding_regs=1024
ngctl connect modbus: lower ng_ksocket:inet/stream/tcp/502
.Ed
.Pp
Talk to it over a virtual transport, one PDU per item, from a test harness:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ngctl create modbus
ngctl config modbus setconfig role=1 transport=1 unit_id=1
.Ed
.Sh CAVEATS
The client role issues one request at a time and does not retry.
A transaction that has no response within
.Dv MODBUS_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_MS
milliseconds is given up and counted in the
.Li timeouts
statistic.
.Pp
No RS-485 direction control is available in the serial drivers, so half
duplex lines need a transceiver with automatic direction control.
.Pp
RTU framing depends on silence to delimit frames.
A frame that is still incomplete when the line has been quiet for
.Ms 3.5
character times is discarded.
The character times are computed from the configured baud rate and bits per
character, and the specification's fixed values are used above 19200 Bd, but a
software timer is not exact: above 19200 Bd the t3.5 gap of 1.750 ms can be
missed or measured late, and this implementation makes no real-time claim.
.Sh TESTS
The protocol engine and the framings are also covered by a host build under
.Pa share/tests/modbus ,
run with
.Dl make run .
It needs neither netgraph nor hardware, and nothing outside the tree: the
engine includes only headers that a host build also has.
.Pp
The node itself is covered by
.Ev "tests/sys/netgraph:ng_modbus" .
That test needs root, needs the module installed so it can be loaded, and
runs as part of the FreeBSD test suite:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make -C /usr/src/sys/modules/modbus
make -C /usr/src/sys/modules/modbus install
make -C /usr/src/tests install
kyua test -k /usr/tests/Kyuafile netgraph:ng_modbus
kyua report
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ngctl 8 ,
.Xr ng_ksocket 4 ,
.Xr ng_tty 4
